# Commands and results

- `go test ./... -count=1`: passed for all Go packages.
- `go vet ./...`: passed.
- `npm test`: passed, 3 tests covering install, Skill backup/management, Windows npm launch, uninstall, and version validation.
- `.local/verify-products.ps1`: passed against the China CDN; returned 9 product combinations, including `wow/12.0.7.68887/68887` with 13 locales.
- `.local/verify-package.ps1`: passed; cross-compiled five supported OS/architecture targets and confirmed all five binaries in the 22-file npm package.
- `.local/verify-doctor.ps1`: passed; doctor returned structured installation, directory, target, cache, lock, temporary-file, CDN, WoWDBDefs, Listfile, and TACT checks.
- Isolated npm integration: global command and managed Skill installed; `--keep-data` retained data while removing binary/Skill; default uninstall removed managed home and Skill.
- `comet native check cli-only-wowdata`: passed; 63 scoped text files scanned, 0 issues.

# Skipped checks

- No real npm registry publish, Git tag push, or GitHub Release was performed. The release workflow was reviewed and the local package/build stages were executed instead.
- Non-Windows binaries were cross-compiled on Windows but not executed on their target operating systems.

# Spec consistency

The implementation matches the confirmed CLI-only specification: CLI target fields have no defaults; Skill supplies `remote/cn/latest/zhCN` while leaving product selection explicit; ordinary queries prepare caches automatically; warmup remains optional; bounded download concurrency defaults to four workers; managed state lives under `~/.wowdata`; npm installs the CLI and text-only Skill; release automation covers the five-platform matrix.

# Known limitations and risks

- Registry credentials, npm provenance, GitHub permissions, and Release creation are validated by workflow structure rather than a production publish.
- China CDN discovery is time-dependent; the recorded Build values are verification observations, not constants in the Skill.

# Conclusion

Pass. All 48 acceptance items have fresh typed evidence, the project test suites pass, real China CDN discovery succeeds, the five supported binaries build, npm package contents are complete, and no blocking findings remain.
